# API Conventions

> Standard API design patterns for {{project.name}}.

## When to Use

Load this skill when designing or implementing any API endpoint.

## Response Format

**Success**:
```json
{
  "data": { ... },
  "message": "optional success message"
}
```

**Error**:
```json
{
  "error": "ERROR_CODE",
  "message": "Human-readable description"
}
```

## HTTP Status Codes

| Code | Use For |
|------|---------|
| 200  | Successful GET, PUT, PATCH |
| 201  | Successful POST (resource created) |
| 204  | Successful DELETE (no body) |
| 400  | Validation error, bad request |
| 401  | Not authenticated |
| 403  | Authenticated but not authorized |
| 404  | Resource not found |
| 409  | Conflict (duplicate, state conflict) |
| 422  | Unprocessable entity |
| 500  | Server error (never expose internals) |

## Endpoint Naming

- Use plural nouns: `/api/users`, `/api/tasks`
- Nest for relations: `/api/projects/:projectId/tasks`
- Use kebab-case: `/api/team-members`
- Actions as sub-resources: `/api/tasks/:id/assign`

## Key Rules

- Every endpoint must validate request body/params/query
- Every response must follow the standard format above
- Never expose internal error details in production
- Use pagination for list endpoints
- Include `Content-Type: application/json` header

